4.1 Connection Description
The proposed 300 kW PV system ties into the customer-owned side of the site's existing electrical service.
Power flow from the three Solmery Power SM-100K-3P inverters is aggregated at the new PV AC
combiner (PVC-1), routed through a lockable utility-accessible AC disconnect (PVD-1), and lands on a
new 400 A back-fed breaker in the existing 480 V main distribution switchboard (MDS-1). MDS-1 is fed
from the plant's existing utility service transformer through the site's existing 480 V main service
disconnect and the existing utility revenue meter.
The new PV interconnection is therefore behind the existing service meter — the same point of common
coupling as the site's existing electrical service — on the load side of the utility revenue meter and
upstream of the plant's process load buses.
Alleniom Utilities · DER Program Office PXA-2025-0244 | DIS-APP-01 | Page 2

No new utility-side equipment, no new service transformer, no new service drop, and no separate revenue
meter is requested. The Applicant proposes to net the PV generation against plant load through the
existing bidirectional revenue meter of record.
